.TH "ABSTRACTMODULESOURCE" "3JS" "September 11, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
AbstractModuleSource \- AbstractModuleSource
.SH SYNOPSIS
An \f[B]\f[BI]AbstractModuleSource\f[B]\f[R] object represents the
compiled source of a module obtained with \f[CR]import source\f[R] or
\f[CR]import.source()\f[R].
There is no directly visible \f[CR]AbstractModuleSource\f[R]
constructor.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \f[CR]AbstractModuleSource\f[R] constructor (often referred to as
\f[CR]%AbstractModuleSource%\f[R] to indicate its \(lqintrinsicness\(rq,
since it does not correspond to any global exposed to a JavaScript
program) serves as the superclass of all module source subclasses,
providing a common interface of utility methods.
This constructor is not directly exposed: there is no global
\f[CR]AbstractModuleSource\f[R] property.
It is only accessible through
\f[CR]Object.getPrototypeOf(moduleSourceObject.constructor)\f[R] and
similar.
.SS AbstractModuleSource objects
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]WebAssembly.Module\f[R]
.PP
JavaScript module source objects will be added by the \c
.UR https://github.com/tc39/proposal-esm-phase-imports
ECMAScript Module Phase Imports
.UE \c
\ proposal.
.SH CONSTRUCTOR
This object cannot be instantiated directly \(em attempting to construct
it with \f[CR]new\f[R] throws a \f[CR]TypeError\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[B]import\f[R] source modSource \f[B]from\f[R] \(dq./module.wasm\(dq;

\f[B]new\f[R] (Object.getPrototypeOf(modSource.constructor))();
\f[I]// TypeError: Abstract class AbstractModuleSource not directly constructable\f[R]
.EE
.PP
Instead, obtain a module source object using \f[CR]import source\f[R],
\f[CR]import.source()\f[R], or a concrete module type\(cqs API, such as
\f[CR]WebAssembly.Module()\f[R].
These mechanisms do not call the abstract constructor.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
These properties are defined on
\f[CR]AbstractModuleSource.prototype\f[R] and shared by all
\f[CR]AbstractModuleSource\f[R] subclass instances.
.TP
\f[B]AbstractModuleSource.prototype.constructor\f[R]
The constructor function that created the instance object.
\f[CR]AbstractModuleSource.prototype.constructor\f[R] is the hidden
\f[CR]AbstractModuleSource\f[R] constructor function, but each module
source subclass also defines its own \f[CR]constructor\f[R] property.
.TP
\f[B]AbstractModuleSource.prototype[Symbol.toStringTag]\f[R]
The initial value of the
\f[CR]AbstractModuleSource.prototype[Symbol.toStringTag]\f[R] property
is a getter that returns a string based on the constructor\(cqs
identity, such as \f[CR]\(dqWebAssembly.Module\(dq\f[R] or
\f[CR]\(dqModuleSource\(dq\f[R].
It returns \f[CR]undefined\f[R] if the \f[CR]this\f[R] value is not an
instance of one of the module source subclasses.
This property is used in \f[CR]Object.prototype.toString()\f[R].
